        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "## No exporters wired yet\n\nThis dashboard currently only scrapes the **backend** Django service via the grafana-agent (see `infra/grafana-agent/agent.yaml`). To populate Postgres, Redis, and Celery panels, the following exporters need to be added as scrape targets:\n\n- **postgres_exporter** \u2014 connection counts, transaction rate, slow queries, replication lag, deadlocks. Run as a Railway service pointed at the Railway-managed Postgres `DATABASE_URL`.\n- **redis_exporter** \u2014 ops/sec, memory usage, evicted keys, blocked clients. Point at `REDIS_URL`.\n- **celery-exporter** (e.g. `danihodovic/celery-exporter`) \u2014 queue depth (most important during M04 webhook spikes), worker count, task durations and failures by task name. Connects to the same Celery broker URL the workers use.\n\nFollow-up issue: file under M10 \u00a76.5 \"Observability polish\" \u2014 these exporters are listed there as part of the full system-health pass. They can also land earlier piecewise if M04 webhook ingest needs the Celery panels sooner.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "title": "Why these panels are empty",
      "type": "text"
    },
